WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.076 --> 00:00:10.865
"I deserve a treat after all that shopping," Cecil said, pausing in front of a smoothie store.

2
00:00:10.866 --> 00:00:17.036
Mia laughed. "Buying new shoes isn't that hard."

3
00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:23.331
Suddenly they heard a commotion behind them, and a female voice yelled, "Help!"

4
00:00:23.332 --> 00:00:28.902
Cecil and Mia turned around and saw a man lying on the ground.

5
00:00:28.903 --> 00:00:32.251
"My husband collapsed!" the woman cried.

6
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:37.562
"I'll dial 9-1-1," Cecil said, pulling out his phone.

7
00:00:37.563 --> 00:00:44.001
The woman dropped to her knees beside her husband. "He's not breathing!"

8
00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:49.484
People gathered around, looking worried, but no one moved to help.

9
00:00:49.485 --> 00:00:54.350
"This is 9-1-1," the operator said. "What is your emergency?"

10
00:00:54.351 --> 00:01:01.999
Cecil told the operator his name and location and explained the situation before passing his phone to the woman.

11
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.040
"I'm Stephanie Hart," she said.

12
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:09.206
She answered a few questions, then her eyes went wide.

13
00:01:09.207 --> 00:01:13.708
"I don't know how to do CPR, but I'll try!"

14
00:01:13.709 --> 00:01:19.795
Cecil put his phone on speaker mode so Mrs. Hart could hear the operator's instructions.

15
00:01:19.796 --> 00:01:24.740
Mrs. Hart put her hands on her husband's chest and began to press.

16
00:01:24.741 --> 00:01:29.333
Soon an ambulance arrived and paramedics jumped out.

17
00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:35.102
One of them quickly checked Mr. Hart before taking over CPR from Mrs. Hart.

18
00:01:35.103 --> 00:01:42.681
Within seconds the man was breathing, and the paramedics put him in the ambulance.

19
00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:45.981
"That was awful," Mia said.

20
00:01:45.982 --> 00:01:49.240
Cecil nodded.

21
00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:54.104
That evening Cecil recounted the frightening episode to his family.

22
00:01:54.105 --> 00:01:58.380
"You did the right thing by calling 9-1-1," Dad said.

23
00:01:58.381 --> 00:02:01.440
"I wanted to do more," Cecil said.

24
00:02:01.441 --> 00:02:08.089
"I've seen two-hour CPR courses with certified instructors at the community college," Dad said.

25
00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.835
Cecil smiled. "Let's sign up!"

26
00:02:12.836 --> 00:02:16.561
Two weeks later Cecil and Dad attended the class.

27
00:02:16.562 --> 00:02:21.728
Miss Reese, the instructor, stood behind a desk in front of the room.

28
00:02:21.729 --> 00:02:27.231
A training dummy of a man's head and torso was propped against the desk.

29
00:02:27.232 --> 00:02:30.966
"CPR saves lives," she began.

30
00:02:30.967 --> 00:02:38.293
"When the heart stops due to something like a heart attack or near drowning, blood circulation stops too.

31
00:02:38.294 --> 00:02:42.487
It only takes minutes for brain damage to occur.

32
00:02:42.488 --> 00:02:47.347
CPR keeps blood flowing to the brain to help prevent damage.

33
00:02:47.348 --> 00:02:51.785
We'll start by learning how to perform CPR on an adult.

34
00:02:51.786 --> 00:02:54.690
Does anyone know what to do first?"

35
00:02:54.691 --> 00:02:59.057
Cecil half-raised his hand, and Miss Reese called on him.

36
00:02:59.058 --> 00:03:02.708
"Call 9-1-1?" he said hesitantly.

37
00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:06.127
"That's right!" the instructor said.

38
00:03:06.128 --> 00:03:09.441
"Why don't you come up and help me demonstrate?"

39
00:03:09.442 --> 00:03:15.761
Dad gave Cecil an encouraging smile, and Cecil made his way to the front of the classroom.

40
00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.988
Miss Reese placed the dummy on the floor.

41
00:03:18.989 --> 00:03:23.208
"First check whether Darrell the Dummy is conscious."

42
00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:29.373
Cecil knelt beside the dummy. "Umm, Darrell? Can you hear me?"

43
00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:33.174
"Darrell's not responsive," Miss Reese said.

44
00:03:33.175 --> 00:03:36.966
"He's definitely unconscious," Cecil agreed.

45
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:42.113
"Next," Miss Reese said, "check if Darrell is breathing."

46
00:03:42.114 --> 00:03:49.239
She showed Cecil how to put his ear near Darrell's mouth and nose to listen for breathing.

47
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:52.470
"He's not breathing," Cecil said.

48
00:03:52.471 --> 00:04:00.230
"Since Darrell is unconscious and not breathing, that means we should perform CPR," Miss Reese said.

49
00:04:00.231 --> 00:04:06.099
"He needs to be on his back on a firm surface, and luckily he already is.

50
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:11.332
Before starting CPR though, we need to make sure his airway is clear.

51
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:16.211
We can't perform CPR if Darrell's airway is obstructed.

52
00:04:16.212 --> 00:04:19.143
Tilt the head back and lift the chin.

53
00:04:19.144 --> 00:04:24.843
Then check inside Darrell's mouth for anything that might cause him to choke."

54
00:04:24.844 --> 00:04:28.901
Cecil did as Miss Reese told him. "It's clear."

55
00:04:28.902 --> 00:04:34.009
"Now we can start chest compressions," Miss Reese said.

56
00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:39.943
Following Miss Reese's instructions, Cecil put a hand in the center of the dummy's chest.

57
00:04:39.944 --> 00:04:42.576
He placed his other hand on top of the first.

58
00:04:42.577 --> 00:04:47.597
With his elbows stiff, he pushed down on the dummy's chest.

59
00:04:47.598 --> 00:04:50.550
"A little harder," Miss Reese said.

60
00:04:50.551 --> 00:04:55.591
"Push five to six centimeters—about a third of the depth of the chest.

61
00:04:55.592 --> 00:05:05.437
Keep going at about 100 to 120 compressions per minute until the person begins breathing or help arrives."

62
00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:10.690
Cecil pushed and pushed—it was hard work!

63
00:05:10.691 --> 00:05:16.283
"He's breathing!" Miss Reese announced to applause from the class.

64
00:05:16.284 --> 00:05:20.236
Dad and the other members of the class took turns saving Darrell.

65
00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:27.232
Cecil even tried another rescue himself, feeling more confident the second time.

66
00:05:27.233 --> 00:05:34.540
After class Cecil and Dad met Mia at the smoothie store and told her about what they had learned.

67
00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:42.609
"It's scary to think that any one of these people could collapse," Mia said, looking out the store windows.

68
00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.967
"It's very unlikely," Dad said.

69
00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:53.178
"I hope I never have to use CPR, but I feel better now that I know what to do," Cecil said.

70
00:05:53.179 --> 00:05:55.746
"Maybe you could take the class too."

71
00:05:55.747 --> 00:06:03.128
Mia smiled. "I'm going to sign up!"

